@startuml use-case-auth
title ADMS - Use Cases: Authentication
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Staff / Superadmin\n(any authenticated user)" as Auth

usecase "Login" as UC_Login
usecase "Logout" as UC_Logout
usecase "Create Session" as UC_CreateSession

Guest --> UC_Login
Auth --> UC_Logout
UC_Login ..> UC_CreateSession : <<include>>

@enduml

@startuml use-case-users
title ADMS - Use Cases: User & Access Management
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Superadmin" as Super

usecase "Register First Account\n(bootstrap superadmin)" as UC_Bootstrap
usecase "View Users" as UC_ViewUsers
usecase "Change User Name /\nEmail / Password" as UC_ChangeBasics
usecase "Add Staff User" as UC_AddUser
usecase "Change User Role" as UC_ChangeRole
usecase "Grant Permission" as UC_Grant
usecase "Revoke Permission" as UC_Revoke
usecase "Delete User" as UC_DeleteUser

Guest --> UC_Bootstrap
Guest --> UC_ViewUsers
Guest --> UC_ChangeBasics
Super --> UC_AddUser
Super --> UC_ChangeRole
Super --> UC_Grant
Super --> UC_Revoke
Super --> UC_DeleteUser

note right of UC_Bootstrap
  Only reachable while the system has
  **zero** users; that first account
  becomes Superadmin unconditionally.
end note

note right of UC_ChangeBasics
  No auth check at all on these three
  endpoints - any Guest can rename or
  re-email or re-password any user id.
end note

note bottom of UC_DeleteUser
  Role change / grant / revoke / delete
  all require an authenticated Superadmin,
  and both role-change and delete refuse
  to remove the **last** superadmin.
end note

@enduml

@startuml use-case-items
title ADMS - Use Cases: Item Management
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest\n(no auth enforced)" as Guest

usecase "Create Item" as UC_CreateItem
usecase "View Items" as UC_ViewItems
usecase "Edit Item Details\n(name / description / status / type)" as UC_EditItem
usecase "Update Item Health" as UC_UpdateHealth
usecase "Record Health Reading" as UC_RecordHealth
usecase "View Item Health History" as UC_ViewHealthHistory
usecase "Delete Item" as UC_DeleteItem

Guest --> UC_CreateItem
Guest --> UC_ViewItems
Guest --> UC_EditItem
Guest --> UC_UpdateHealth
Guest --> UC_ViewHealthHistory
Guest --> UC_DeleteItem

UC_CreateItem ..> UC_RecordHealth : <<include>>\n(initial reading)
UC_UpdateHealth ..> UC_RecordHealth : <<include>>\n(append, never overwrite)

note bottom of UC_RecordHealth
  Health readings are append-only - a
  change never overwrites a prior value,
  which is what powers the trend chart
  behind "View Item Health History".
end note

@enduml

@startuml use-case-warehouses
title ADMS - Use Cases: Warehouse Management
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest\n(no auth enforced)" as Guest

usecase "Create Warehouse" as UC_CreateWarehouse
usecase "View Warehouses" as UC_ViewWarehouses
usecase "Rename Warehouse" as UC_RenameWarehouse
usecase "Add Item to Warehouse" as UC_AddItemToWarehouse
usecase "Remove Item from Warehouse" as UC_RemoveItemFromWarehouse
usecase "Delete Warehouse" as UC_DeleteWarehouse

Guest --> UC_CreateWarehouse
Guest --> UC_ViewWarehouses
Guest --> UC_RenameWarehouse
Guest --> UC_AddItemToWarehouse
Guest --> UC_RemoveItemFromWarehouse
Guest --> UC_DeleteWarehouse

note bottom of UC_AddItemToWarehouse
  An item can belong to more than one
  warehouse in the data model - nothing
  enforces "one warehouse per item".
end note

@enduml

