@startuml use-case-tenders
title ADMS - Use Cases: Tender Management
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest\n(no auth enforced)" as Guest

usecase "Create Tender" as UC_CreateTender
usecase "View Tenders" as UC_ViewTenders
usecase "Add Item to Tender" as UC_AddItemToTender
usecase "Edit Tender Details\n(title / description / status)" as UC_EditTender
usecase "Set Tender Winner" as UC_SetWinner
usecase "Conclude Tender" as UC_ConcludeTender
usecase "Delete Tender" as UC_DeleteTender

Guest --> UC_CreateTender
Guest --> UC_ViewTenders
Guest --> UC_AddItemToTender
Guest --> UC_EditTender
Guest --> UC_SetWinner
Guest --> UC_ConcludeTender
Guest --> UC_DeleteTender

UC_ConcludeTender ..> UC_SetWinner : <<include>>
UC_ConcludeTender ..> UC_EditTender : <<include>>\n(status -> OVER)

note bottom of UC_EditTender
  Status changes have no transition
  guard - any status can move to any
  other status, including backward
  (e.g. OVER back to NOT_PUBLISHED).
end note

@enduml

@startuml use-case-organization
title ADMS - Use Cases: Organization Settings
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest\n(no auth enforced)" as Guest

usecase "View Organization Settings" as UC_ViewOrg
usecase "Update Organization Settings" as UC_UpdateOrg

Guest --> UC_ViewOrg
Guest --> UC_UpdateOrg

note bottom of UC_UpdateOrg
  Singleton record (fixed id = 1); GET
  never 404s, PUT upserts. Feeds the
  printable tender poster template on
  the frontend.
end note

@enduml

@startuml use-case-reports
title ADMS - Use Cases: Reporting
skinparam actorStyle awesome

actor "Guest" as Guest
actor "Staff / Superadmin\n(any authenticated user)" as Auth

usecase "View Stock Reports" as UC_ViewReports
usecase "Print / Export Tender Poster" as UC_TenderPoster
usecase "Generate Stock Report" as UC_GenerateReport

Guest --> UC_ViewReports
Guest --> UC_TenderPoster
Auth --> UC_GenerateReport

note right of UC_GenerateReport
  The only write endpoint in the whole
  backend besides Users' role/permission/
  delete actions that requires @CurrentUser
  (any authenticated user, not just
  Superadmin). Produces a frozen snapshot,
  not a live-recomputed view.
end note

@enduml
